{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"19 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,15.629,3.651,3.268,"PVR INOX"],[13.889,14.731,34.055,2.373,2.124,"A record quarter, already in the price"],[13.889,20.845,52.954,1.809,1.634,"PVR INOX is up 18% since Q2 results on 28 October (NIFTY 11%) and 68%"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"this year, a 52-week high. The quarter was its biggest: income ₹2,133 cr, up"],[13.889,23.733,52.951,1.809,1.634,"17%; EBITDA ₹448 cr before other income (₹475 cr as the company reports it),"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"up 44%; net profit ₹273 cr, up 111%. Admissions rose only 4%, to 46.3m. ATP"],[13.889,26.621,52.936,1.809,1.634,"₹298 and spend per head ₹153 rose 14%, occupancy reached 30.4% against"],[13.889,28.065,52.934,1.809,1.634,"28.7%, and 51 paise of every extra half-year rupee reached EBITDA, lifting H1's"],[13.889,29.509,52.934,1.809,1.634,"margin to 17.6% from 12.7%. Other income of ₹28 cr from reversed provisions"],[13.889,30.954,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and a ₹21 cr cut to depreciation flattered it; neither explains a 21.3% margin"],[13.889,32.421,9.692,1.809,1.634,"against 17.3%."],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"We model H2 income up 14% at a 17.4% margin, below H1's 17.6% and Q2's"],[13.889,36.328,52.964,1.809,1.634,"21.3%, giving FY27E EBITDA of ₹1,333 cr (FY26: ₹872 cr) and EPS of"],[13.889,37.772,52.964,1.809,1.634,"₹74.30. That is 38% above consensus of ₹53.69, which implies H2 net profit of"],[13.889,39.216,52.951,1.809,1.634,"₹172 cr, a 4.5% margin and less than Q2 alone: the screen predates the results."],[13.889,40.684,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Screens grow from 1,797 to 1,868 by March and 2,033 a year later, mostly asset-"],[13.889,42.128,52.964,1.809,1.634,"light builds; we grow revenue 11% and 10% and hold the margin flat. Capex of"],[13.889,43.572,52.931,1.809,1.634,"₹310 cr against ₹1,333 cr of EBITDA turns September's ₹141 cr of net cash into"],[13.889,45.016,17.014,1.809,1.634,"₹1,101 cr by March 2028."],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our target of ₹1,730 averages two methods. Five listed exhibitors trade at a"],[13.889,48.946,52.951,1.809,1.634,"median 10.3x EV/EBITDA (CNK 9.4x, MCS 9.5x, CGX 10.3x, AMC 12.2x,"],[13.889,50.39,52.934,1.809,1.634,"IMAX 14.2x), giving ₹1,638 on the next twelve months' EBITDA. A ten-year"],[13.889,51.834,52.954,1.809,1.634,"DCF at a 12% cost of equity and 5.5% terminal growth gives ₹1,827; at 11-13%"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the range is ₹2,145-1,594. The legs bracket the price: the multiple says the"],[13.889,54.722,52.957,1.809,1.634,"market already pays for the recovery; the price needs 8% annual free-cash-flow"],[13.889,56.167,52.957,1.809,1.634,"growth to FY37, against 9% forecast. Consensus targets average ₹1,688, below"],[13.889,57.611,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the price; 17 of 18 ratings are buy. Q3 holding Q2's margin, or a screen pipeline"],[13.889,59.055,33.16,1.809,1.634,"earning its cost of capital, would change our mind."],[13.889,61.542,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,70.154,1.489,1.022,0.915,"500"],[14.451,67.792,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[14.451,65.443,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,500"],[14.451,63.083,2.306,1.022,0.915,"2,000"],[18.061,70.848,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.684,70.848,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.471,70.848,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.243,70.848,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.826,72.043,4.868,1.275,1.111,"PVR INOX ("],[22.697,72.069,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[23.31,72.043,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[26.394,72.043,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.291,73.179,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.561,73.179,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.279,73.179,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,73.179,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,74.244,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.372,74.244,2.811,1.387,1.209,"68.2%"],[24.09,74.244,2.811,1.387,1